# Change Log Content Generation

When the user asks for a **web** or **mobile** change log / release notes / version update text:

1. Read `CHANGELOG.md` at the repo root (and the Flutter app copy `lion-roaring-app/CHANGELOG.md` when that workspace is open) for the **last versions** and prior entries.
2. Determine platform: `web` or `mobile` (or both if “today’s updates”).
3. Cross-check Site Settings (`WEB_APP_VERSION`, `MOBILE_APP_VERSION`) and recent git commits; do not invent features.
4. Propose a **new version number** (semver bump from the last version in `CHANGELOG.md`) unless the user already specified one.
5. Return ready-to-paste Change Log content in this exact structure:

```
Platform: Web Version | Mobile App Version
Version: vX.Y.Z
Type: feature | improvement | bugfix | security
Title: Short release title
Description:
- Bullet 1
- Bullet 2
- Bullet 3
```

6. **Always update `CHANGELOG.md`** in the same turn: bump the Current versions table and prepend the new entry under Entries (newest first). Mark status `draft (ready to publish)` until the user confirms it was published in PMA; then set `published` and sync the “Last published” line. Keep web and Flutter `CHANGELOG.md` copies identical when both repos are in the workspace.
7. If the user asks you to **apply** it, then:
   - Update Site Settings version (`WEB_APP_VERSION` or `MOBILE_APP_VERSION`) via Change Logs management (not Site Settings UI).
   - Create a `change_logs` row (or tell them to paste into PMA Change Logs → Add Entry) with matching platform/version/title/type/description. Prefer HTML lists (`<ul><li>…</li></ul>`) for the description field.
   - Mark the matching `CHANGELOG.md` entry as `published`.
   - Update `docs/pma/change-logs.md` only if product behavior changed beyond the note itself.
8. Keep tone clear and user-facing (PMA members read these notes).
